,"after":{"work_id":324,"title":"Emma","language":"dut","open_library_edition_id":"OL24354728M","isbn_13":"9789027491428","isbn_10":null,"publisher":"Het Spectrum"}},{"ref":"d2","relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","key":{"work_id":324,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":324,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":3,"text":"Emma Woodhouse is jong, welgesteld en overtuigd van haar inzicht in andere mensen. Ze bemoeit zich graag met hun liefdesleven en verwacht met haar koppelpogingen het beste voor hen te bereiken. Haar voorstellingen blijken echter niet altijd overeen te komen met wat anderen voelen of willen. In de sociale wereld om haar heen krijgen kleine vergissingen grote betekenis. Jane Austen volgt hoe Emma gaandeweg wordt geconfronteerd met de beperkingen van haar oordeel en met haar eigen gevoelens.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Gecontroleerde boek- en catalogusbronnen","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL66513W","evidence":[{"type":"reviewed_identity_and_bibliography","sources":["http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p851671039"],"reference":"work:324","checked_at":"2026-11-02T19:50:00.000Z","note":"Austen’s complete novel Emma, C.W.Polderman-deVries translation, Spectrum hardcover. No film retelling or new Work. Current1815original year retained;1816on later title-page/bibliographic citations is not automatically a correction. New Dutch full-novel edition does not overwrite the unverified legacy edition.","supplemental":null},{"type":"original_substantive_source_review","review":"content-review-017.json","sources":["https://openlibrary.org/works/OL66513W","https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p851671039"]},{"type":"cover_front_review","cover_id":6579542,"sha256":"8d61ef0c1da111e60cfeaf3a277653551c0a7e237facbf15c2a13d7b59e82b82","reference":"cover-semantic-review-010.json","limitation":"Actually read cover-large/sheet-002.jpg. Jane Austen; Emma; Kramers Klassieken. Front identity and source-edition attachment are corrobor