-20261102-012"}},{"ref":"e3","relation":"editions","key":{"open_library_edition_id":"OL24405542M"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":331,"title":"De storm","language":"dut","open_library_edition_id":"OL24405542M","isbn_13":"9789035108363","isbn_10":null,"publisher":"Bert Bakker"}},{"ref":"d3","relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","key":{"work_id":331,"language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":331,"language":"nl","bound_author_id":196,"text":"Op een afgelegen eiland leeft Prospero met zijn dochter Miranda, ver van het hertogdom dat hem is afgenomen. Met behulp van zijn kennis en macht roept hij een storm op die vroegere tegenstanders naar het eiland brengt. Hun aankomst geeft hem gelegenheid de verhoudingen te veranderen. Illusie, verlangen en macht bepalen vervolgens de ontmoetingen tussen de eilandbewoners en de schipbreukelingen. Het toneelstuk onderzoekt wat iemand met controle over anderen doet wanneer herstel en vergelding dicht bij elkaar liggen.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Gecontroleerde boek- en catalogusbronnen","source_url":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL362699W","evidence":[{"type":"reviewed_identity_and_bibliography","sources":["http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p067411541"],"reference":"work:331","checked_at":"2026-11-02T19:50:00.000Z","note":"Exact Dutch play TheTempest. GerritKomrij is translator, Shakespeare remains primary author. Full Shakespeare play in Komrij translation, never infer print language or completeness from the legacy educational edition.","supplemental":null},{"type":"original_substantive_source_review","review":"content-review-017.json","sources":["https://openlibrary.org/works/OL362699W","https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p067411541"]},{"type":"cover_front_review","cover_id":6666745,"sha256":"a3b0bfc7d8b56ac429b392194e12db98f593b8595d45c14cd291840de096b389","reference":"cover-semantic-review-010.json","limitation":"Actually read cover-large/sheet-002.jpg. William Shakespeare; De storm; Gerrit Komrij